---
import { JpgComponent } from "../components/jpg.component";
import Layout from "../layout/Layout.astro";
const title = 'Convert HEIC to JPG Online — Individual Photos or Batch ZIP';
const description = 'Convert HEIC photos to JPG in your browser. Save individual JPEG images or a batch ZIP, with local photo processing and no account.';
const ogImage = "/og-image/heic-to-jpg.png";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} ogImage={ogImage} ogTitle={title}>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4">
    <h1 class="text-center font-bold text-4xl mt-12 mb-5">Convert HEIC to JPG</h1>
    <p class="text-center text-zinc-700 mb-8">Make JPEG copies for a recipient or form that accepts JPG. Each selected HEIC becomes a separate JPG; Download All packages the images in a ZIP.</p>
    <JpgComponent client:visible />
    <section class="mt-12 mb-10 prose max-w-none" aria-labelledby="conversion-steps">
      <h2 id="conversion-steps">How to convert HEIC to JPG</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Choose <strong>Choose files</strong> and select the HEIC photos on your device.</li>
        <li>Wait for conversion to finish. It starts automatically after selection.</li>
        <li>Select a finished preview to save that image, or choose Download All for a ZIP of the separate results.</li>
        <li>Check the downloaded result before sharing it. Choose <strong>Convert More</strong> to start another batch.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Selected photo bytes are processed locally in your browser rather than uploaded to a conversion server. The website still loads its scripts and other web resources. No account or conversion fee is required.</p>
      <p>For alternatives and troubleshooting, read the <a href="/blog/heic-to-jpg/">HEIC to JPG guide</a> and <a href="/how-it-works/">how conversion works</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose max-w-none mb-10" aria-labelledby="conversion-limits">
      <h2 id="conversion-limits">What to check before using the result</h2>
      <p>JPEG uses lossy compression. This converter uses a fixed quality setting and has no quality slider, resize or target-file-size controls. The result is a sharing copy rather than a complete archive of the HEIC and its metadata.</p>
      <p>Large photos or batches can need substantial memory. If conversion fails, try a single complete HEIC file, then a smaller batch. Support can vary with the HEIC variant, browser and available device memory.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose max-w-none mb-16" aria-labelledby="format-choice">
      <h2 id="format-choice">When to choose JPG</h2>
      <p>Check the recipient's accepted formats, maximum file size and pixel dimensions. JPG and JPEG are the same image format, but changing a HEIC filename to .jpg does not convert it. Open the downloaded file and keep your source photo.</p>
      <p>Compare <a href="/blog/heic-jpg-png-pdf-which-format/">JPG, PNG, WebP and PDF</a>, or use the <a href="/blog/heic-photo-upload-not-supported/">photo upload checklist</a> if a form still rejects your file.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
